    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0916" n="904" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg904"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/5–246: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-05-02T19:00:00+02:00">May 2, 1946—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 3—2:51 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>499. Embassy’s telegram 489, May 1.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d709-f1"/> I presented
                    proposed Lend-Lease settlement<anchor n="31" xml:id="d709-f2"/> to Foreign
                    Minister this morning. We went over question in some detail. Saka said he fully
                    shared desire reach settlement soon as possible and hoped to set an example so
                    far as Turkey <pb facs="0917" n="905" xml:id="pg905"/> is concerned. He said
                    proposal would be studied immediately by government experts.</p>
                <p>I expect see Prime Minister<anchor n="32" xml:id="d709-f3"/> and Minister Finance
                    shortly regarding this matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d709-f1" n="30" xml:id="d709-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d709-f2" n="31" xml:id="d709-f2-content">
                <p>Since March 29, the Department had been in communication with the Embassy in
                    Turkey on this subject; details not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d709-f3" n="32" xml:id="d709-f3-content">
                <p>Sükrü Saraçoğlu.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
